\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Control flow of the candidate search of \texttt  {SynthesizeJointBestOf}. The upper loop draws $N$ candidates and keeps the one with the highest joint score $S$ of Equation~\ref {eq:syn-score}; the lower loop attempts at most three repairs, each a fresh draw of the whole line with the two weakest characters pinned to the anchor, and accepts one only when $S$ strictly improves, so a repair that fixes a letter at the cost of the writer's identity is rejected. Both judges score the same rendered ink, the classifier after the stroke normalisation of Section~\ref {sec:wid-strokenorm}.}}{56}{figure.caption.34}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:syn-search}{{10}{56}{Control flow of the candidate search of \texttt {SynthesizeJointBestOf}. The upper loop draws $N$ candidates and keeps the one with the highest joint score $S$ of Equation~\ref {eq:syn-score}; the lower loop attempts at most three repairs, each a fresh draw of the whole line with the two weakest characters pinned to the anchor, and accepts one only when $S$ strictly improves, so a repair that fixes a letter at the cost of the writer's identity is rejected. Both judges score the same rendered ink, the classifier after the stroke normalisation of Section~\ref {sec:wid-strokenorm}}{figure.caption.34}{}}
