\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces End-to-end result per writer over all thirteen writers: writer identification and character accuracy, both measured through the G-code round trip, for three novel sentences per writer at best-of-8 (\texttt  {gcode\_v2\_summary.json}; shape judge \texttt  {author\_shape\_10new\_weights}, text judge \texttt  {paper\_cnn\_bilstm\_ctc\_joint\_best}). Ten of the thirteen writers are identified at 100\% by the shape judge; the remaining three are 150 at 33.3\% and Abhinav and Yeukita at 66.7\% each. The character-accuracy failures are concentrated in the two writers whose hands are the most joined, which is the known weak case of an exemplar synthesiser that cuts letters apart and reassembles them.}}{108}{figure.caption.70}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:res-e2e}{{22}{108}{End-to-end result per writer over all thirteen writers: writer identification and character accuracy, both measured through the G-code round trip, for three novel sentences per writer at best-of-8 (\texttt {gcode\_v2\_summary.json}; shape judge \texttt {author\_shape\_10new\_weights}, text judge \texttt {paper\_cnn\_bilstm\_ctc\_joint\_best}). Ten of the thirteen writers are identified at 100\% by the shape judge; the remaining three are 150 at 33.3\% and Abhinav and Yeukita at 66.7\% each. The character-accuracy failures are concentrated in the two writers whose hands are the most joined, which is the known weak case of an exemplar synthesiser that cuts letters apart and reassembles them}{figure.caption.70}{}}
