\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces Layer shapes and trainable parameters of the text recogniser (batch dimension omitted). A convolution with batch normalisation holds $C_{\mathrm  {out}}(9C_{\mathrm  {in}}+1)+2C_{\mathrm  {out}}$ parameters and one LSTM direction $4n(I+n)+8n$ with $n=256$, which is where every entry comes from. Of the total the LSTM layers hold 70.5\,\%, stage~3 24.2\,\%, stage~2 3.9\,\%, the output layer 1.1\,\% and stage~1 0.3\,\%. Batch normalisation also stores 2\,176 non-trainable running statistics, so a checkpoint holds $3\,358\,763+2\,176=3\,360\,939$ numbers, 13.4\,MB as 32-bit floating point.}}{113}{table.caption.95}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rec-layers}{{28}{113}{Layer shapes and trainable parameters of the text recogniser (batch dimension omitted). A convolution with batch normalisation holds $C_{\mathrm {out}}(9C_{\mathrm {in}}+1)+2C_{\mathrm {out}}$ parameters and one LSTM direction $4n(I+n)+8n$ with $n=256$, which is where every entry comes from. Of the total the LSTM layers hold 70.5\,\%, stage~3 24.2\,\%, stage~2 3.9\,\%, the output layer 1.1\,\% and stage~1 0.3\,\%. Batch normalisation also stores 2\,176 non-trainable running statistics, so a checkpoint holds $3\,358\,763+2\,176=3\,360\,939$ numbers, 13.4\,MB as 32-bit floating point}{table.caption.95}{}}
