\newlabel{fig:sty-code}{{36}{122}{The two routines of the builder that locate each character, as pseudocode. The first is Equation~\ref {eq:sty-viterbi}: it differs from the CTC loss of Equation~\ref {eq:rec-alpha} in taking the maximum where the loss takes a sum, which is what turns a probability into a single best alignment, and it keeps back-pointers so that the path itself can be recovered. The second is the cut cost of Equation~\ref {eq:sty-cut} evaluated for every column, which is minimised near the boundary to place the cut at a ligature, that is at a column that is both thin and low}{figure.caption.116}{}}
