\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {37}{\ignorespaces The four routines of the motion program as pseudocode. In \texttt  {StepSegment}, \texttt  {delay} is $\tau $ of Equation~\ref {eq:gan-tau} and \texttt  {e} is the error term of Equation~\ref {eq:gan-bres}; the end-stop read before every major-axis pulse is what sets the latency of Equation~\ref {eq:gan-latency}. In \texttt  {Calibrate}, \texttt  {N} and the two assignments after it are the quantities of Equation~\ref {eq:gan-cal}. \texttt  {SetPen} must check the switch first because the cam turns one way only, so an unnecessary pulse would toggle the pen to the wrong state rather than leave it alone.}}{129}{figure.caption.131}\protected@file@percent }
